<title>CHINA: Capital Asia year net returns to profit.</title>
<headline>Capital Asia year net returns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   2.86 gain    vs 8.9 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0	    vs 0.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  7.76 loss    vs 15.46 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    13.29 profit vs 38.50 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		     731.82	 vs 497.08</p>
<p>    Company name		 Capital Asia Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 23-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 13</p>
<p>NOTE - Capital Asia is a property investment and financial services group.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss of HK$2.69 million on provision for doubtful debts, loss of HK$3.85 million on provision for diminution in value of an associated company, loss of HK$6.74 million on provision for permanent diminution in value of long term investments and gain of HK$5.52 million on disposal of long-term investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is one H.K. cent vs 0.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
